{{also|erde}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|erde}}, from {{inh|de|goh|erda}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*erþu}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*erþō}}. Compare {{cog|nl|aarde}}, {{cog|fy|ierde}}, {{cog|en|earth}}, {{cog|da|jord}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌸𐌰}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈeːrdə/|[ˈʔeːɐ̯də]|[ˈʔɛɐ̯də]}}
* {{rhymes|de|eːɐ̯də}}
* {{audio|de|de-Erde.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|Erde|Erden}}

# {{lb|de|uncountable}} [[soil]]
#: {{ux|de|Sie nahm eine Handvoll '''Erde'''.|t=She took a handful of '''soil.'''|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|uncountable}} the [[ground]]
#: {{ux|de|Er fiel auf die '''Erde'''.|t=He fell on the '''ground.'''|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|countable}} a [[world]]; a space to live in
#: {{ux|de|Diese '''Erde''' wird vergehen, aber Gott wird eine neue '''Erde''' schaffen.|t=This '''earth''' will fade, but God will create a new '''earth.'''}}

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-f|n}}
* Dative singular can also be {{m|de|Erden}} in older texts and phrases as {{m|de|auf Erden}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|ground}} {{l|de|Boden}}; {{l|de|Grund}}
